From 5288dd43d3fbf853cbf65a1a1c10414f06fc1f04 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: legsmechanical <joshgaine@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 4 Jun 2026 10:51:46 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat(fx): shared send preset list + preset save/load fixes

- Send A and Send B now share ONE preset store (single presets_send dir +
  send_preset_* keys); both descriptors point at it. (Old per-bus dirs
  presets_send_a/_b abandoned; start fresh.)
- Generic "[Save Preset]" label (was "[Save MFX Preset]").
- Per-bus loaded-preset name (fxBusPresetName), stashed/restored on bus switch
  in enterFxBusEditor, so a master preset (e.g. SPECTRA) no longer preselects
  overwrite on a send save.
- Fix preset serialization corruption with gap patterns (filled/empty/filled):
  json_get_section_bounds skipped past a null-valued slot and grabbed the next
  slot's object (e.g. CT -- AW -- saved as CT AW AW AW). Now anchors on the
  key's colon and only reads an object when the value actually is one. Also
  fixes the same latent bug in master presets.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
